I am the creator of Page Rage (
https://page-rage.com/
), which I released about two weeks ago. Page Rage didn't get too much traction on Hacker News (
https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49746963
), but it did end up being a top post on r/webdev (
https://www.reddit.com/r/webdev/comments/1whepc7/page_rage_d...
) and r/playmygame (
https://www.reddit.com/r/playmygame/comments/1whfp3g/my_firs...
)
The linked project "Destroy any website" makes it's own distinct creative and gameplay choices. It may have been inspired by Page Rage or it may have been a case of "multiple discovery". Either way, "Destroy any website" is not a low quality slop clone, it's clearly had a lot of thought put into it
